{
  "area": "skills-unlocks",
  "description": "What a node COSTS, what it ASKS and whether an actor may take it (US-3 of `123-skill-trees-and-progression`). Each case carries the whole input — the authored node with its parents, its goals, its cost and its effects, the actor’s pool for that node’s tree, whether they already hold it, and the fully resolved SkillTuning. `expected.requirements` is the single gate this module evaluates: an authored `skill_node_requires/2` goal verbatim, plus one `skill_unlocked(Actor, Parent)` per authored parent edge, deduplicated and canonically sorted — tree STRUCTURE and a reputation check are the same mechanism, which is what lets a tree gate on anything the KB knows. `expected.resolution.conditional` is separate from `available` on purpose: a node may be both, meaning nothing core knows refuses it and something core cannot evaluate might. Refusals are evaluated in SKILL_UNLOCK_REFUSALS order — unknown, owned, points — and neither `requires` nor `forbidden` ever appears in a pinned resolution, because both are the rules layer’s; `trees.json` is where they show up, since a view is handed the KB’s answers rather than guessing them. Regenerate with `npm run skill-resolution-corpus`.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a-root-node-with-nothing-in-its-way",
      "note": "The base case: no parents, no authored goals, a pool that affords it. `conditional` is false, which is the only state in which core has settled an unlock entirely on its own.",
      "input": {
        "actor": "wren",
        "node": {
          "parents": [],
          "requires": [],
          "effects": [
            {
              "kind": "modifies",
              "args": [
                "damage",
                2
              ]
            }
          ],
          "id": "true_chisel",
          "tree": "stonework",
          "name": "True Chisel",
          "cost": 1
        },
        "points": 3,
        "unlocked": false,
        "tuning": {
          "pointsPerLevel": 1,
          "defaultNodeCost": 1,
          "defaultMaxLevel": 10,
          "levelXp": [
            0,
            0,
            100,
            250,
            450,
            700,
            1000,
            1350,
            1750,
            2200,
            2700
          ],
          "advanceAction": "train_skill",
          "unlockAction": "unlock_skill_node"
        }
      },
      "expected": {
        "resolution": {
          "actor": "wren",
          "node": "true_chisel",
          "tree": "stonework",
          "points": 3,
          "action": "unlock_skill_node",
          "cost": 1,
          "requires": [],
          "conditional": false,
          "available": true
        },
        "requirements": [],
        "cost": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a-parent-desugars-into-the-goal-gate",
      "note": "THE case the vocabulary turns on. An authored `parents` edge becomes `skill_unlocked(Actor, true_chisel)` in `requires`, so there is ONE gate to evaluate and a host still gets the edge to draw. A port with a node-graph walker beside a goal evaluator has two.",
